data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 11 (EF Core 11), the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. All synchronous LINQ operators and `SaveChanges()` now throw `InvalidOperationException` unconditionally.

**All four methods break:**

| Method | Throws on |
|--------|-----------|
| `GetAll()` | `.ToList()` |
| `GetById()` | `.First()` |
| `GetCount()` | `.Count()` |
| `Save()` | `.SaveChanges()` |

## The Fix

Convert to async throughout:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Why:** The Cosmos DB SDK is async-only. The previous "sync" path was always just `.GetAwaiter().GetResult()` internally, risking deadlocks. EF Core 11 removes that workaround entirely — async is now mandatory for the Cosmos provider.
